WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:03.690
amyotrophic Lateral sclerosis

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:06.960
Shortened to Als is a neurodegenerative disease

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:11.099
Which usually begins in adulthood and Advances rapidly?

00:00:11.559 --> 00:00:15.599
It's characterized by the deterioration and loss of both upper and lower

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:18.150
motor Neurons as

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:22.979
the motor Neurons stop sending signals the Muscles weaken leading to Paralysis

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:29.820
When the muscles in the diaphragm are paralyzed this can be fatal. There is no known cure for Als

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:37.499
For most people the cause of their lS is unknown, but some people inherit the disease from their parents

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:41.009
By studying the genes that are altered in these patients

00:00:41.739 --> 00:00:46.378
scientists have pinpointed processes in the neurons that might be causing als

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:53.039
It's too early to [know] which of these altered processes are a result of the disease and which could be a cause

00:00:53.379 --> 00:00:57.569
But it's clear that they affect many different aspects of the motor neuron function

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:05.970
Let's start in the cell body here proteins that are not transported into the nucleus build up in the cytoplasm

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:11.699
Errors in the systems that build up and break down proteins also cause other

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:14.220
[Misfolded] proteins to accumulate

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:19.470
The different proteins can then aggregate and can become toxic to cells in Several ways

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:24.989
For example they can damage mitochondria the cell's power generators

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:32.189
Mitochondrial damage can lead to oxidative stress which can trigger breaks in the dNA of the cell

00:01:32.979 --> 00:01:36.479
Als seems to affect Dna repair processes as well

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:42.570
When Dna breaks are poorly repaired it ultimately contributes to the death of the neuron?

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:46.140
the cells Transport Machinery can also be damaged

00:01:46.659 --> 00:01:50.129
For example [als] affected neurons often have problems

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:52.570
Transporting rnA

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:54.189
proteins and

00:01:54.189 --> 00:01:55.570
vesicles

00:01:55.570 --> 00:02:02.639
Both in the cytoplasm and along the neurons axon these vesicles containing [Pourtant] cell signaling molecules called neurotransmitters

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:09.330
If these can't be moved along the axon or released the neuron can't send messages to its target cells

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:11.320
damage to the

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:14.070
cytoskeleton can also cause the Axon to retract [if]

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:20.939
This happens the Axon can no longer connect to the muscle nearby and can no longer signal the muscle to contract

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:24.930
other cell types can also be involved in als

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:33.029
Oligodendrocytes which electrically insulate the axon and [provide] support to the motor neuron don't work in people with Als

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.280
reduced uptake of

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:43.020
Neurotransmitters by astrocytes can lead to over activation of the receptors at the synapse and death of the neuron

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:49.950
Finally astrocytes and Microglia can produce factors that protect or [damaged] motor neurons

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:54.480
Neuronal death occurs when excessive damaging factors are produced

00:02:55.600 --> 00:03:02.549
Further research is needed to find out which of these many processes caused the motor neuron degeneration seen in als patients

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:10.020
Targeting new drug therapies at those processes might lead to a treatment for this incurable disease

